{"name":"White Pointer","hex":"#dad6cc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white pointer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Carcharodon carcharias, a species of shark."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white_pointer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Great white shark","blocks":[{"text":"The great white shark, also known as the white shark, white pointer, or great white, is a large shark. It is closely related to the mako sharks, the porbeagle, and the salmon shark. It is a robustly built species with a grayish upperside and a white underside. The white shark is one of the largest living shark and fish species, though it is still smaller than the whale shark and basking shark. It has about 300 triangular, serrated teeth that are continuously replaced. Its massive, fatty liver can reach over a quarter of its body weight, providing buoyancy and storing energy. The species is partially warm-blooded, an adaptation that allows it to remain active in colder waters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/White_shark.jpg/330px-White_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_white_shark"},{"title":"Pointer (dog breed)","blocks":[{"text":"The Pointer, sometimes called the English Pointer, is a medium-sized breed of pointing dog developed in England. Pointers are used to find game for hunters, and are considered by gundog enthusiasts to be one of the finest breeds of its type; however, unlike most other hunting breeds, its purpose is to point, not retrieve game."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/English_Pointer_orange-white.jpg/330px-English_Pointer_orange-white.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pointer_(dog_breed)"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg/500px-Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg/1280px-Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg/500px-Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Evolution from C. hastalis to C. carcharias","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEvolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Great_White_Shark_%2814730744390%29.jpg/500px-Great_White_Shark_%2814730744390%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Great_White_Shark_%2814730744390%29.jpg/1280px-Great_White_Shark_%2814730744390%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Great_White_Shark_%2814730744390%29.jpg/500px-Great_White_Shark_%2814730744390%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm